# Architecture

## Layers

- **Frontend** (`frontend/`) — Next.js UI, browser behavior, and HTTP API
  consumption
- **Backend** (`backend/`) — NestJS API, domain logic, and server-side
  integrations
- **AI worker** (`worker-proxy-agent-ia/`) — isolated worker process for the
  AI execution boundary
- **Power BI integration** (`ms-powerbi-embedded/`) — Python service reached
  through the backend
- **Infrastructure** (`infrastructure/`) — Docker Compose, Dockerfiles, and
  local PostgreSQL

## Constraints

- The frontend must never access the database directly.
- Business logic belongs in backend services, not frontend components or
  controllers.
- Validate external input at the backend HTTP boundary.
- Follow `docs/conventions.md` for file placement.
- Follow an approved `tasks/specs/` specification for feature scope, behavior,
  and acceptance criteria.
- Use `docs/product.md` and `docs/design.md` for durable global decisions.
- Update `docs/api.md`, `openapi.yaml`, and Swagger at `/api/docs` when an
  approved feature changes the HTTP contract.
- Update `docs/database.md` when an approved feature changes the persistent
  model.
- Adopt TypeORM, PWA support, authentication, and external integrations only
  when the product requires them.

## Communication

```text
Browser -> Next.js -> NestJS API -> Persistence when required
```

